    "description": "The Tepees in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petrified_Forest_National_Park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Petrified Forest National Park\">Petrified Forest National Park</a> in northeastern <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arizona\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Arizona\">Arizona</a>, United States. View is toward the northwest from the main park road. According to a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Park_Service\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:National Park Service\">National Park Service</a> (NPS) <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.nps.gov/pefo/naturescience/geologicformations.htm\">document</a>, rock strata exposed in the Tepees area of the park belong to the Blue Mesa Member of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinle_Formation\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Chinle Formation\">Chinle Formation</a> and are about 220 to 225 million years old. The colorful bands of mudstone and sandstone were laid down during the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triassic\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Triassic\">Triassic</a>, when the area was part of a huge <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.nature.nps.gov/geology//paleontology/pub/fossil_conference_6/lucas.htm\">tropical floodplain</a>.",
